 ## Overview
-BLMCA is a hybrid mesh-cell assignment heuristic for tiled parallel volume rendering that simultaneously minimizes communication volume during the Ray-Segment Migration (RSM) step and mitigates load imbalance during the Local Pixel Merging (LPM) step [S1, unofficial]. It improves upon pure Minimum-Communication Assignment (MCA) by incorporating load-balancing constraints, and improves upon pure Best-Fit Decreasing (BFD) load balancing by prioritizing communication efficiency for heavily loaded cells [S1, unofficial]. It is chosen when both inter-processor communication overhead and computational load imbalance are critical bottlenecks [S1, unofficial].
+BLMCA is a hybrid mesh-cell assignment heuristic for tiled parallel volume rendering that simultaneously minimizes communication volume during the Ray-Segment Migration (RSM) step and mitigates load imbalance during the Local Pixel Merging (LPM) step [S1, unofficial]. It improves upon pure Minimum-Communication Assignment (MCA) by incorporating load-balancing constraints, and improves upon pure Best-Fit Decreasing (BFD) load balancing by prioritizing communication efficiency for heavily loaded cells [S1, unofficial]. This scheme considers both the volume of communication in the RSM step and the load imbalance in the LPM step for minimization [S1, unofficial].
 
